---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Topbar from '../components/Topbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Vox0 privacy policy" description="How Vox0 handles microphone audio, dictation, local settings and model downloads.">
  <Topbar show />
  <main id="main" class="privacy">
    <header class="hero privacy-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <img class="mark" src="/images/logo.png" alt="" width="256" height="256" />
        <p class="eyebrow">Vox0 · Privacy policy</p>
        <h1>Privacy,<br /><span class="lime">by design.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">Your voice and dictations stay on your PC. Here’s what Vox0 stores locally and when it connects to the internet.</p>
        <ul class="privacy-facts" aria-label="Privacy at a glance">
          <li>No audio uploads</li>
          <li>No account</li>
          <li>No developer analytics</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="privacy-date">Developed by Bryan Ramirez · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-24">October 24, 2026</time></p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap narrow privacy-layout">
      <article class="privacy-copy" aria-label="Privacy policy">
        <section id="voice">
          <h2>Your voice and text stay on your PC</h2>
          <p>Vox0 processes microphone recordings locally with Whisper. It does not upload
            audio or transcriptions to the developer or an online transcription service.
            The microphone records while you hold your configured push-to-talk key.
            Recordings are processed in memory, not saved as audio files.</p>
          <p>Vox0 types the resulting text into the focused editable field. It uses
            Windows accessibility to identify that field and sends Unicode keyboard
            input. It does not read the field's existing text or access your clipboard.
            Recent dictations remain in the application's in-memory history until you
            close it. The application receiving the text handles it under its own policy.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="local-data">
          <h2>Local data</h2>
          <p>Settings and a bounded performance log are stored in
            the MSIX package's private <code>LocalState</code> folder under
            <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Packages</code>.
            The log includes technical information such as timings, model and device
            details and transcription character counts, never the dictated text.
            Vox0 does not automatically send this log anywhere.</p>
          <p>The MSIX stores its downloaded speech models in that same private folder.
            Updates preserve this data. Uninstalling the new MSIX removes its settings,
            logs and downloaded models. Reinstalling starts with default settings and
            requires downloading a model again. External model folders selected by you
            are not deleted. Older releases may have left data outside the package.</p>
          <p>The source Development app uses its own profile in
            <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Vox0Development</code> and the Python environment's
            model cache; uninstalling the MSIX does not remove development data.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="connections">
          <h2>Internet connections</h2>
          <p>Internet is needed to download speech models from Hugging Face, including
            a download needed to repair an incomplete cache. That service receives
            normal connection information, such as your IP address and requested model.
            Audio and dictation are not included. Once a working model is downloaded,
            dictation can run offline.</p>
          <p>Vox0 requires no account and includes no advertising or developer analytics.
            Microsoft Store installation and updates are handled by Microsoft under
            its own privacy policy.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="website">
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>The website is hosted on Vercel. Hosting providers may process connection
            and request data to serve and protect the site. The site stores your theme
            preference locally in your browser. It does not receive dictation from Vox0.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="contact" class="privacy-contact">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions, use the
            <a href="https://github.com/bryramirezp/vox0/issues">Vox0 support tracker</a>.
            Issues are public; do not include private recordings, dictations or secrets.</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-hero { padding: 116px 0 60px; }
  .privacy-hero .mark { width: 64px; height: 64px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .privacy-hero .lede { max-width: 33em; margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .privacy-facts {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 10px 24px;
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 22px;
    color: var(--title); font-size: .88rem;
  }
  .privacy-facts li::before { content: '✓'; color: var(--accent-text); margin-right: 7px; }
  .privacy-date { color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; margin: 0; }
  .privacy-layout {
    padding-top: 54px; padding-bottom: 76px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .privacy-copy { min-width: 0; }
  .privacy-copy section { padding: 34px 0; scroll-margin-top: 88px; }
  .privacy-copy section:first-child { padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
  .privacy-copy h2 { font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.7vw, 1.6rem); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .privacy-copy p { line-height: 1.8; }
  .privacy-copy section > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .privacy-copy code {
    padding: 2px 5px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--panel); color: var(--title); font: .8em var(--mono);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .privacy-copy .privacy-contact {
    margin-top: 12px; padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px; background: var(--tint);
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .privacy-hero { padding: 104px 0 42px; }
    .privacy-layout { padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 48px; }
    .privacy-copy section { padding: 28px 0; }
  }
</style>
